# Laravel conventions

- Test-first (AITooling `tdd`): write the failing Pest/PHPUnit test before the code
  (`php artisan make:test XTest --pest`). Every feature/endpoint/bug fix has a test; no test, not done.
- Detect the Laravel + PHP version from `composer.json`; never use APIs missing from it.
- Prefer `php artisan make:*` generators over hand-written boilerplate.
- Migrations: always create with `php artisan make:migration` (or `make:model -m`), then edit the generated file. Never hand-write a migration from scratch; always define a reversible `down()`.
- Laravel Boost is not installed and must not be added; read `composer.json`, `database/migrations/` and `routes/` directly (use a Boost MCP server only if your agent already exposes one).
- Validation: Livewire components use `#[Validate]` + `$this->validate()`; HTTP controllers use inline `$request->validate()` for one or two fields and a Form Request once rules are shared or grow. Authorization in policies/gates.
- Domain writes go through `app/Actions/*` (one class per use case, authorizing inside); simple reads stay as Eloquent calls. No service/repository layers.
- Set `$fillable`/`$guarded` deliberately (mass-assignment safety).
- Match sibling files' style; don't introduce new patterns unless the project already uses them.
- Before "done": run Pint and Pest through `./bin/pf shell` (`./bin/pf shell ./vendor/bin/pint --test`, `./bin/pf shell php artisan test`). Larastan/PHPStan only if a `phpstan.neon` exists (it does not today).

Full guidance: `ai/skills/laravel-generate/SKILL.md`.
